====================================================================================================
v112  CONVERGENCE PER TOTAL SHOT
====================================================================================================
  Heisenberg N=4, M=16, exact ground state -6.464102, 20 epochs, 3 seeds.
  Identical step rule and R schedule in every arm; only the marked thing differs.
  TIER A for gradients and steps; energies reported by Statevector.

   budget     arm                                 spent      energy         gap
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    1.3e+05   V6            (flat shots)      1.31e+05    -5.9327    +0.5314   [5s]
    1.3e+05   p-shift       (flat shots)      1.31e+05    -6.0436    +0.4205   [16s]
    1.3e+05   p-shift  (ANNEALED shots)       1.30e+05    -5.9610    +0.5031   [17s]

    1.0e+06   V6            (flat shots)      1.05e+06    -5.9906    +0.4735   [10s]
    1.0e+06   p-shift       (flat shots)      1.05e+06    -6.0152    +0.4489   [20s]
    1.0e+06   p-shift  (ANNEALED shots)       1.05e+06    -6.0568    +0.4073   [20s]

====================================================================================================
READING IT
====================================================================================================
   budget        A: V6      B: PS flat   C: PS annealed     A-B        C-B
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    1.3e+05     -5.9327     -6.0436      -5.9610      +0.1109    +0.0826
    1.0e+06     -5.9906     -6.0152      -6.0568      +0.0246    -0.0417

  A - B is the ESTIMATOR at matched total shots, matched step rule, matched
  schedule. NEGATIVE means V6 reaches a lower energy for the same shots -
  which would contradict v109/v110's per-point reading and show that
  gradient quality was never the binding constraint.

  C - B is what SHOT ANNEALING alone buys parameter-shift. If C reaches A,
  the advantage is the schedule, not the multiplexing, and V6's real
  contribution is packaging rather than physics.

  Both matter. A win on A-B that survives C is the strongest form of the
  claim this project can make on the shot axis, and it has never been
  measured because the benchmark matches shots PER CIRCUIT.

  Scope: one problem, one N, 3 seeds, 20 epochs, one R schedule which was
  tuned for V6 and is therefore charged against parameter-shift too.
